---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const description="Couriers cross a shifting storm field. Their instruments are noisy, packets arrive late, and a regional bias can make a whole neighborhood sincerely wrong. Four teams have the same bodies and sensors; only their treatment of evidence changes.";
const path='/intelligence/agent-swarm/shared-reality/';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:"Shared Reality",description,url:'https://iamrobin.ai'+path,learningResourceType:'Interactive simulation',inLanguage:'en'};
const content="<div class=\"swarm-lab\"><a class=\"lab-back\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/\">← Agent Swarm Lab</a><p class=\"lab-kicker\">Field study 02 / 06 · Shared Reality</p><header class=\"lab-head\"><h1>Many maps.<br><em>One weather.</em></h1><p class=\"lab-deck\">Nobody sees the whole storm. Everyone has an instrument. Several instruments can be wrong in exactly the same way.</p></header><p class=\"lab-zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">很多地图，同一场风雨。</p><section class=\"lab-stage\" data-swarm-model=\"/agent-swarm/shared-reality/\" aria-label=\"Shared Reality interactive simulator\">\n <div class=\"lab-stage-top\"><span><i class=\"lab-live-dot\"></i>OBSERVATORY / 02</span><span>Seeded simulation · evaluator view</span></div>\n <div class=\"lab-grid\"><div class=\"lab-view\"><canvas class=\"lab-world\" data-world aria-label=\"Animated orthographic 3D sketch of simulator states. Current and final measures are available in the table below.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-camera\"><button type=\"button\" data-camera>Plan / 3D</button><button type=\"button\" data-rotate>Rotate ↻</button></div></div>\n <aside class=\"lab-side\"><label>Treatment<select data-arm aria-label=\"Treatment\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-readout\"><strong data-live-value>—</strong><span data-live-label>Net useful work</span></div><p class=\"lab-event\" data-event>Observe. Compare. Change one assumption.</p><p class=\"small\">Node color and height = predicted risk (green → amber). The field shows evaluator truth.</p><div class=\"lab-checks\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-compare/>Compare all</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-trails checked/>Trails</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-signals checked/>Links</label></div><label>Inspect a body<select data-agent aria-label=\"Agent to inspect\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-inspect\" data-inspect><p class=\"small\">Click a body in the world, or choose it here. This is an evaluator view of recorded state.</p></div></aside></div>\n <div class=\"lab-buttons\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" data-play aria-pressed=\"false\">Play world</button><button type=\"button\" data-replay>Replay ↺</button><button type=\"button\" data-end>Final tick →</button><button type=\"button\" data-next-seed>Next seed</button><button type=\"button\" data-download>Save this run ↓</button></div>\n <label class=\"lab-timeline\"><span class=\"tiny\">Time</span><input data-timeline aria-label=\"Simulation timeline\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"0\"/><output data-time>0 ticks</output></label>\n <p class=\"lab-status\" data-status role=\"status\">Loading the model. Recorded evidence remains available below.</p>\n <div class=\"lab-controls\"><div><label>Choose a world<select data-preset aria-label=\"World preset\"></select></label><p data-preset-note></p><button type=\"button\" data-apply>Run these parameters →</button></div><form class=\"lab-params\" data-params aria-label=\"World parameters\"></form></div>\n <div class=\"lab-scores\"><p class=\"tiny\">Net useful work / units · higher is better</p><canvas data-curve class=\"lab-curve\" aria-label=\"Measured outcome over time for each treatment. Dashed markers identify interventions.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Treatment</th><th>At this tick</th><th>At mission end</th></tr></thead><tbody data-scores></tbody></table></div></div>\n <noscript><p>JavaScript is needed to run the simulator. Read the saved multi-seed evidence and method below.</p></noscript>\n </section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">01 / Try to break it</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Make them agree. Then make them wrong.</h2><p>Watch source-aware gossip beside echoed consensus. Choose “Shared delusion” to bias a whole region’s sensors. Then break the radio. Compare useful trips with forecast error: agreement alone does not deliver a parcel.</p><blockquote class=\"lab-hypothesis\">Can agents agree enough to act without agreeing confidently on a mistake?</blockquote></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">02 / The mechanism</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>What the little world actually does.</h2><p>Couriers predict the risk of their next trip from local readings and delivered messages. Evidence carries source, sensing time, variance and expiry. The naive treatment repackages posteriors as fresh evidence; source-aware gossip retains origins. A central collector must receive reports and send its estimates back through fallible links.</p><p>The colored field is the evaluator’s view. Couriers do not receive it. Their world model is tested through an action and a prediction of its outcome, so a tidy shared database cannot count as intelligence by itself.</p><p lang=\"zh-Hans\" class=\"lab-zh\">传感器带噪声，消息会延迟，多个个体也可能共享同一种误差。这里同时测量任务结果、预测误差与错误共识。图中的全局风险属于评估器，行动者只能使用实际得到的观测与消息。</p></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">03 / Recorded evidence</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Keep the inconvenient outcomes.</h2><p><strong>Provenance did not establish an overall useful-work advantage over echoed consensus. It improved forecast quality with stale maps, but a shared sensor bias could still fool it. The declared superiority criterion did not pass. Missing consensus trials remain missing, with the valid denominator retained.</strong></p><p>Source-aware, expiring evidence should resist repeated rumors, but cannot repair a common sensor failure or manufacture observations across a partition.</p><p class=\"small\">Paired seeded simulations. Every retained result can be regenerated from the versioned source; these are synthetic experiments, not field validation.</p><details class=\"lab-batch\"><summary>Inspect every world and treatment</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><caption class=\"tiny\">Net useful work · mean by predeclared world</caption><thead><tr><th>World / treatment</th><th>Mean units</th><th>n</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Patchy weather / Private observations</th><td>898.67</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Patchy weather / Echoed consensus</th><td>949.33</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Patchy weather / Source-aware gossip</th><td>933.83</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Patchy weather / Bounded collector</th><td>931.46</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Broken radio / Private observations</th><td>898.67</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Broken radio / Echoed consensus</th><td>948.54</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Broken radio / Source-aware gossip</th><td>946.92</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Broken radio / Bounded collector</th><td>874.42</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Shared delusion / Private observations</th><td>757.54</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Shared delusion / Echoed consensus</th><td>790.13</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Shared delusion / Source-aware gossip</th><td>775.08</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Shared delusion / Bounded collector</th><td>770.21</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Yesterday’s map / Private observations</th><td>937.17</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Yesterday’s map / Echoed consensus</th><td>926.29</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Yesterday’s map / Source-aware gossip</th><td>940.88</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Yesterday’s map / Bounded collector</th><td>925.46</td><td>24</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><p class=\"small\">One chosen seed is an illustration. The downloadable batch retains every world and treatment; null means unavailable. A confidence interval describes the sampled synthetic worlds, not the real world.</p><div class=\"lab-links\"><a href=\"/agent-swarm/shared-reality/results.json\" download>All recorded runs ↓</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/shared-reality/README.md\">Method &amp; reproduction</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/shared-reality/model.mjs\">Read the model</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/shared-reality/source.zip\" download>Source package ↓</a></div></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section lab-method\"><p class=\"tiny\">04 / Inspect the boundary</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Enough detail to disagree.</h2><details><summary>Inputs, budgets and observation boundaries</summary><dl data-audit></dl></details><details><summary>Every measure in the current run</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\" data-summary></div></details><ul><li>A synthetic two-dimensional risk field, illustrated in 3D; not a weather or human-belief model.</li><li>All couriers know station coordinates and their own location; risk and future outcomes are hidden.</li><li>The provenance treatment assumes honest source identities. It is not Byzantine consensus.</li><li>A common-mode sensor error can fool every method. Agreement is not ground truth.</li></ul><p class=\"small\">3D sketching adds depth to the explanation. It does not add an unmodeled physical dimension, extra sensor data or unearned intelligence to the experiment.</p></div></section><nav class=\"lab-next\"><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/roach-emergence/\">← Roach Emergence</a><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/learn-forget-evolve/\">Learn, Forget, Evolve →</a></nav></div>";
---
<BaseLayout title="Shared Reality — Agent Swarm Lab — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/agent-swarm/lab.css"/>
<Fragment set:html={content}/>
<script is:inline type="module" src="/agent-swarm/client.mjs"></script>
</BaseLayout>
